{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r48.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Round 48, Claude's own reflection (written before reading Codex's report)\n     2\t\n     3\t## The result as registered\n     4\t\n     5\t- 36 scored first attempts, 36 diagnostic retries, $0.3677 spent of $0.50 (ledger: 72 attempts, no refusal by the ledger, not stopped).\n     6\t- All 72 answers were refused by `calc_check.py`; nothing was published. Every attempt finished (status `answered`), so the result is\n     7\t  complete, not INCOMPLETE.\n     8\t- By D725's lines: the joint arm is usable in 0 of 9 pairs. **STOP.**\n     9\t- The blind reading cannot change this. The registered reader brief says a card with no answer cannot be usable, and every card is\n    10\t  \"no answer\". The readers are not run; the packets can still be rendered and sealed at no cost if the record needs them.\n    11\t\n    12\t## What the result measures\n    13\t\n    14\tIt does not measure the question the gate was built for (does judging a family in one call give better numbers than judging each\n    15\tmember alone?). It measures whether the model can fill v13's answer format as the request states it. It cannot.\n    16\t\n    17\t## The mechanism (traced on stored answers, both journals)\n    18\t\n    19\t1. **The format's rules live in the check, not in the request.** The sent schema has 7 descriptions (`what`, `basis`, `kind`,\n    20\t   `expression`, `relation`, `bridge`, `reference`). These fields have none: `value`, `low`, `high`, `bound`, `unit`, `evidence`,\n    21\t   `component`, `inputs`, `operation`, `signs`, `disputed`, `basis_text`, `rests_on`, `converts`, `scenario`, and `outcome` and `rung` on\n    22\t   the answers. The check enforces closed conventions on them that the request never states:\n    23\t   - `evidence` is a passage id, while the model wrote the sentence (175 figures in the first attempts);\n    24\t   - `outcome` and `reference.figure` are figure ids, while the model wrote \"$398.1 billion\" and sentences (45 and 39);\n    25\t   - `bridge` is a figure id, while its own description reads as prose (\"an estimate stating the conversion …\"), and the model\n    26\t     wrote prose (49);\n    27\t   - `unit` must be exactly `USD bn`, `%`, `x` or `USD`; the model wrote `USD billions`, `$ billion`, `percent` and `fraction`;\n    28\t   - a figure has a value or a range, never both; a guidance \"$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\" was read as value, low, high,\n    29\t     bound `approx` and component `midpoint`;\n    30\t   - a period is labelled `FY2027 H1`, not \"FY2027 first half\" or \"first six months\";\n    31\t   - a percentage is applied with `share` (which divides by 100), not `product`;\n    32\t   - `range_from_relative` takes the midpoint and the relative figure as two operands;\n    33\t   - `signs` exists only on `sum` and `roll_forward`, and a four-term difference is a `sum` with signs.\n    34\t2. **Even with these corrected mechanically on copies, nothing publishes.** 9 of 36 first attempts get past the structural layer, and\n    35\t   0 publish. The next layer includes:\n    36\t   - the expression copied with its words (\"65% growth in Q4\", where the extractor yields \"65%\");\n    37\t   - the period vocabulary;\n    38\t   - `apply_growth` of last year's quarter by a year-over-year growth. The check accepts this without a bridge only when the family\n    39\t     has a `same_base` relation, and the bridge description's list of identities does not include growth;\n    40\t   - some arithmetic that follows from the conventions above.\n    41\t3. **One wrong answer anywhere refuses the whole answer.** An answer carries about 20 figures, and each figure must pass several\n    42\t   rules. A long conjunction fails by chance even when each part is usually right (AGENTS §7.1, \"a conjunction over many items fails\n    43\t   by chance\"). The retries carried every reason, and they fixed nothing: 36 of 36 were refused again, mostly on the same classes (prose where an id\n    44\t   is expected in 20, value and range in 22).\n    45\t\n    46\t## My process error\n    47\t\n    48\t- AGENTS §6: \"Check before the send, at no cost. Write one answer that follows the prompt and run every code check on it.\"\n    49\t  - I wrote the $0 gate's answer knowing the check's conventions. It proved that the check accepts a conforming answer, not that\n    50\t    the request teaches one.\n    51\t  - The step that would have caught this at no cost: an answer written by a reader who sees only the request, run through the\n    52\t    checks.\n    53\t- REQUEST-AUDIT.md says \"field definitions moved to the schema\". Only 7 descriptions reached the sent schema, and I did not check the\n    54\t  sent bytes against that sentence.\n    55\t- The eight council rounds (47 to 47h) reviewed the harness: the journals, the keys, the packets and the verdict. None reviewed the\n    56\t  request as the model reads it against the check.\n    57\t- The \"rests_on prose\" diagnosis I gave Alex mid-run was wrong in its field. The prose sat in `bridge`, `evidence`, `outcome` and\n    58\t  `reference`, not in `rests_on`. I correct it in the report.\n    59\t\n    60\t## The way forward (my lean, to be challenged)\n    61\t\n    62\t- The gate as registered says STOP. It is recorded as written (D680).\n    63\t- What the result can still decide: whether a v13-style calculation can be filled at all. That decides whether the number-answer\n    64\t  work continues on this path.\n    65\t- Lean:\n    66\t  - **(ii) first:** move every decision code can make out of the model.\n    67\t    - Code extracts each numeric expression from the shown passages and lists it as a numbered source figure, with value, unit,\n    68\t      bound and period parsed by code. The model only references these by id. This removes the expression, evidence, unit and\n    69\t      value-or-range classes at their owner.\n    70\t    - `outcome`, `reference.figure`, `bridge`, `inputs` and `evidence` become enums of the ids the request holds where the strict\n    71\t      schema allows it.\n    72\t  - **(i):** every remaining field gets its rule in the schema beside it, including the operation and period vocabulary, and the\n    73\t    check's too-narrow rules are written down as decisions before any change.\n    74\t  - **The test, all at $0 before any send:**\n    75\t    - every stored answer is re-read under the changed contract, and no right answer may be refused;\n    76\t    - a blind reader who sees only the new request writes answers for three families, and they must pass;\n    77\t    - then the same 36-request gate, about $0.40, on Alex's word.\n    78\t  - **Stop condition:** if a blind reader's answers still fail on rules the request states, the format is too heavy for one call.\n    79\t    In that case close judging-v13 and keep poc-v118 (D690).\n    80\t- Not certain:\n    81\t  - (ii) is a new design piece (code builds the source figures), not a wording fix. It needs its own design tables (AGENTS §2)\n    82\t    before code.\n    83\t  - Whether Alex wants to spend more on this path is his call.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py | sed -n '26,132p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py | sed -n '16,117p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py | sed -n '26,132p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py | sed -n '16,117p'\"","aggregated_output":"    26\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    27\timport calc_check as cc                                                 # noqa: E402\n    28\timport render_v13 as rv                                                 # noqa: E402\n    29\tfrom hivemind import config, model                                      # noqa: E402\n    30\t\n    31\tRUN = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\n    32\tCONFIG = REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'                              # its re-judging model setting: gpt-6-luna, medium, 16000 output tokens\n    33\tSYSTEM = (HERE / 'judging-v13-draft.txt').read_text()\n    34\tAPPROVED_CEILING = 0.5                                                  # Alex, 2026-11-22 (D732): \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\"\n    35\tPINNED_PLAN_SHA256 = (HERE / 'paid-plan.sha256').read_text().strip() if (HERE / 'paid-plan.sha256').exists() else None\n    36\tAUTH = Path.home() / '.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/authorization.json'\n    37\tDRAWS = (1, 2, 3)\n    38\tRETRY_MARK = '\\n\\nThe code refused the previous answer because: '\n    39\tPAIRS = [('old-1', ('v4', 9014), ('v8', 9022)), ('old-2', ('v14', 8729), ('v9', 8737)), ('old-3', ('v3', 9183), ('v35', 9177))]\n    40\tSINGLETONS = [('O', 'old-2', 'v29', 8734, ('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', 'company', 'end of FY2027')),\n    41\t              ('S', 'old-2', 'v6', 8595, ('four largest AI hyperscalers', 'data-center capex', 'combined', 'CY2027')),\n    42\t              ('E', 'old-3', 'v41', 9166, ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Vera CPU', 'FY2028'))]\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tdef W(population, measure, scope, period):\n    46\t    return {'population': population, 'measure': measure, 'scope': scope, 'period': period}\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tdef bands(draw, view_id):\n    50\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    51\t    rows = conn.execute('select lo, hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,)).fetchall()\n    52\t    return [[lo / 1e9 if lo is not None else None, hi / 1e9 if hi is not None else None] for lo, hi in rows]\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef passages(draw, evidence_ids):\n    56\t    \"\"\"What each request showed of a passage: the quote cut at 400 characters (judging._lines_english).\"\"\"\n    57\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    58\t    rows = conn.execute(f'select evidence_id, quote, speaker from evidence where evidence_id in ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(evidence_ids))})',\n    59\t                        evidence_ids).fetchall()\n    60\t    return {e: {'text': (q or '')[:400], 'speaker': s} for e, q, s in rows}\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef pair_family(draw, total, dc):\n    64\t    return {'members': {total[0]: {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027'), 'bands': bands(draw, total[0])},\n    65\t                        dc[0]: {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'bands': bands(draw, dc[0])}},\n    66\t            'relations': [{'type': 'part_of', 'part': dc[0], 'whole': total[0]}],\n    67\t            'shared': [W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'), W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q4')],\n    68\t            'compare_periods': ['FY2027 Q3', 'FY2027 Q4', 'FY2027']}\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\tdef only(family, view_id):\n    72\t    return {'members': {view_id: family['members'][view_id]}, 'relations': [], 'shared': family['shared'], 'compare_periods': []}\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\tdef questions(draw, view_ids):\n    76\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    77\t    out = {}\n    78\t    for v in view_ids:\n    79\t        q = conn.execute('select question from views where view_id=?', (v,)).fetchone()[0]\n    80\t        ladder = [c for (c,) in conn.execute('select condition from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (v,))]\n    81\t        out[v] = {'question': q, 'ladder': ladder}\n    82\t    return out\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tdef shown_lines(user):\n    86\t    \"\"\"Each evidence item exactly as the request showed it: its header line (tier, speaker, original source and date) and its quote.\"\"\"\n    87\t    m = re.search(r'\\[Evidence in view for the family, \\d+ items\\]\\n(.*?)(?:\\n\\n\\[|\\n\\nAnswer per)', user, re.S)\n    88\t    out = {}\n    89\t    for chunk in re.split(r'\\n(?=- e\\d+ )', m.group(1) if m else ''):\n    90\t        if chunk.startswith('- e'):\n    91\t            out[chunk[2:].split(' ', 1)[0]] = chunk\n    92\t    return out\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\tdef item(unit, arm, draw, calls, family, shown):\n    96\t    archive = RUN / draw / 'prod/archive.sqlite'\n    97\t    user, evidence_ids, theme_ids = rv.render(archive, calls, family, shown=shown)\n    98\t    return {'unit': unit, 'arm': arm, 'draw_store': draw, 'members': sorted(shown), 'system': SYSTEM, 'user': user,\n    99\t            'schema': rv.v13_schema(sorted(shown), evidence_ids, theme_ids), 'family': family, 'passages': passages(draw, evidence_ids),\n   100\t            'evidence_ids': evidence_ids, 'questions': questions(draw, sorted(shown)), 'shown': shown_lines(user)}\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\tdef build_plan():\n   104\t    items = []\n   105\t    for draw, total, dc in PAIRS:\n   106\t        family = pair_family(draw, total, dc)\n   107\t        calls = [total, dc]\n   108\t        items.append(item(f'pair-{draw}', 'joint', draw, calls, family, [total[0], dc[0]]))\n   109\t        for member in (total, dc):                            # the same union of evidence, one member's header and answer\n   110\t            items.append(item(f'pair-{draw}', f'separate-{member[0]}', draw, calls, only(family, member[0]), [member[0]]))\n   111\t    for name, draw, view_id, call_id, what in SINGLETONS:\n   112\t        family = {'members': {view_id: {'what': W(*what), 'bands': bands(draw, view_id)}}, 'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []}\n   113\t        items.append(item(f'single-{name}', 'single', draw, [(view_id, call_id)], family, [view_id]))\n   114\t    return items\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\tdef plan(out):\n   118\t    items = build_plan()\n   119\t    report = []\n   120\t    for it in items:\n   121\t        missing = sorted(set(it['evidence_ids']) - set(it['passages']))\n   122\t        report.append(f'{it[\"unit\"]:14} {it[\"arm\"]:14} members {it[\"members\"]} user {len(it[\"user\"])} chars, evidence {len(it[\"evidence_ids\"])}, '\n   123\t                      f'schema {len(json.dumps(it[\"schema\"]))} chars, passages missing {missing or \"none\"}')\n   124\t        if missing or 'Outcome keys' not in it['user']:\n   125\t            raise SystemExit(f'{it[\"unit\"]} {it[\"arm\"]}: incomplete request; not planned')\n   126\t    ids = [(i['unit'], i['arm']) for i in items]\n   127\t    if len(set(ids)) != len(ids):\n   128\t        raise SystemExit('duplicate (unit, arm) in the plan; not planned')\n   129\t    text = json.dumps(items, indent=1)\n   130\t    Path(out).write_text(text)\n   131\t    Path(out).with_suffix('.sha256').write_text(hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest() + '\\n')\n   132\t    print('\\n'.join(report))\n    16\tS, N = {'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'number'}\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tdef nullable(schema):\n    20\t    return {'anyOf': [schema, {'type': 'null'}]}\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\tdef obj(props, desc=None):\n    24\t    out = {'type': 'object', 'properties': props, 'required': list(props), 'additionalProperties': False}\n    25\t    if desc:\n    26\t        out['description'] = desc\n    27\t    return out\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\tdef v13_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\n    31\t    what = obj({k: S for k in ('population', 'measure', 'scope', 'period')},\n    32\t               'What the number measures: population, measure (the quantity, such as revenue or units; never its basis), scope, period.')\n    33\t    figure = obj({\n    34\t        'id': S, 'what': what,\n    35\t        'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.BASES - {'prior_forecast'}), 'description': 'reported: an actual; guidance: the company\\'s '\n    36\t                  'outlook; consensus: analysts\\' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this family\\'s forecast.'},\n    37\t        'scenario': S,\n    38\t        'kind': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['computed', 'estimate', 'source'], 'description': 'source: stated in a shown passage; computed: one '\n    39\t                 'operation on named figures; estimate: your judgement, stated as yours.'},\n    40\t        'value': nullable(N), 'low': nullable(N), 'high': nullable(N),\n    41\t        'bound': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['>', '>=', '<', '<=', 'approx', 'approx_below', 'approx_above']}),\n    42\t        'unit': S,\n    43\t        'evidence': nullable(S),\n    44\t        'expression': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Source only: the complete numeric expression exactly as the passage writes '\n    45\t                                'it, qualifiers included (for example \"more than $2 billion\", \"$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%\", \"more than triple\").'}),\n    46\t        'component': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['value', 'bound', 'midpoint', 'relative', 'low', 'high', 'multiplier']}),\n    47\t        'inputs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    48\t        'operation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.OPERATIONS)}),\n    49\t        'signs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': N}),\n    50\t        'relation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['time_aggregation', 'accounting_parts', 'stated_in_addition', 'overlap_unknown'],\n    51\t                              'description': 'Sum and roll_forward: periods of one quantity; declared parts of a whole; a source says they add; '\n    52\t                              'unknown overlap (name the disputed figure).'}),\n    53\t        'disputed': nullable(S),\n    54\t        'bridge': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Only when no listed identity covers the operation (periods of one quantity, '\n    55\t                            'declared parts, a balance and its flows, a stated share or multiplier, a total over a per-unit price): an '\n    56\t                            'estimate stating the conversion and listing the operands it converts.'}),\n    57\t        'basis_text': nullable(S), 'rests_on': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    58\t        'adjusts': nullable(obj({'figure': S, 'type': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['discount', 'uplift', 'trim']}})),\n    59\t        'converts': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    60\t    })\n    61\t    push = obj({'evidence_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    62\t    theme_push = obj({'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': theme_ids or ['none']},\n    63\t                      'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    64\t    answer = obj({\n    65\t        'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': member_ids},\n    66\t        'shape': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['forecast', 'unresolved']},\n    67\t        'outcome': nullable(S), 'rung': nullable({'type': 'integer'}),\n    68\t        'reference': nullable(obj({'figure': nullable(S), 'unavailable': nullable(S)}, 'An external figure, or a calculation from external '\n    69\t                              'and reported figures, or unavailable with why.')),\n    70\t        'reasons': S, 'why': nullable(S),\n    71\t        'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}},\n    72\t        'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': push}, 'theme_pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': theme_push},\n    73\t    })\n    74\t    return obj({'figures': {'type': 'array', 'items': figure}, 'answers': {'type': 'array', 'items': answer}})\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef parts(user):\n    78\t    head, rest = user.split('\\n\\n[Evidence in view', 1)\n    79\t    evidence = '[Evidence in view' + rest.split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0]\n    80\t    tail = '\\n\\n[' + rest.split('\\n\\n[', 1)[1] if '\\n\\n[' in rest else ''\n    81\t    blocks = {b.split(']', 1)[0]: '[' + b for b in tail.split('\\n\\n[')[1:]}\n    82\t    return head, evidence, blocks\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tdef render(archive_path, calls, family, shown=None):\n    86\t    \"\"\"The v13 user message for a family from its members' stored requests: the members in `shown` (default: all) get a header; the\n    87\t    evidence in view is the union over every call, each passage once; the themes once; each member's exact figure keys.\"\"\"\n    88\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{archive_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    89\t    heads, lines, seen, themes, earlier = [], [], set(), '', []\n    90\t    shown = set(shown) if shown is not None else {v for v, _ in calls}\n    91\t    for view_id, call_id in calls:\n    92\t        user = json.loads(archive.execute('select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?', (call_id,)).fetchone()[0])['messages'][1]['content']\n    93\t        head, evidence, blocks = parts(user)\n    94\t        if view_id in shown:\n    95\t            heads.append(head)\n    96\t        for item in evidence.split('\\n- ')[1:]:\n    97\t            eid = item.split(' ', 1)[0]\n    98\t            if eid not in seen:\n    99\t                seen.add(eid)\n   100\t                lines.append('- ' + item)\n   101\t        themes = themes or next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Themes')), '')\n   102\t        prev = next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Previous')), '').split('\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema')[0]   # [46g.1] v7's output line goes\n   103\t        earlier.append(f'- {view_id}: ' + prev.replace('[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]', 'our earlier forecast, not a source:').strip())\n   104\t    rel = '; '.join(f'{r[\"part\"]} is part of {r[\"whole\"]}' if r['type'] == 'part_of' else f'{r[\"later\"]} rests on {r[\"earlier\"]}\\'s base'\n   105\t                    for r in family['relations'] if {r.get('part'), r.get('whole'), r.get('later'), r.get('earlier')} - {None} <= shown) or 'none'\n   106\t    shared = '; '.join(f'{w[\"population\"]}, {w[\"measure\"]}, {w[\"scope\"]}, {w[\"period\"]}' for w in family['shared']) or 'none'\n   107\t    keys = '; '.join(f'{v} = {m[\"what\"][\"population\"]} | {m[\"what\"][\"measure\"]} | {m[\"what\"][\"scope\"]} | {m[\"what\"][\"period\"]}'\n   108\t                     for v, m in family.get('members', {}).items() if v in shown)\n   109\t    user = ('[Family] members:\\n' + '\\n\\n'.join(heads) + f'\\n\\nRelations: {rel}.\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: {shared}.\\n'\n   110\t            + (f'Outcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), to be used exactly: {keys}.\\n' if keys else '') + '\\n'\n   111\t            f'[Evidence in view for the family, {len(lines)} items]\\n' + '\\n'.join(lines) + '\\n\\n' + themes\n   112\t            + '\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.')   # D728: no earlier forecast\n   113\t    return user, sorted(seen), [t.split(' ', 1)[0] for t in themes.split('\\n- ')[1:]]\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\tdef strict(calc, schema):\n   117\t    \"\"\"Fill every optional field with null, as strict structured output returns it.\"\"\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '326,388p'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3711,3718p;11145,11185p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '326,388p'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3711,3718p;11145,11185p'\"","aggregated_output":"   326\t### 7.3 Iterating\n   327\t\n   328\t- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n   329\t  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n   330\t  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n   331\t  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n   332\t- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n   333\t  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n   334\t  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n   335\t  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n   336\t- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n   337\t  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n   338\t  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n   339\t- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n   340\t  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n   341\t- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n   342\t  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n   343\t  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n   344\t  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n   345\t  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n   346\t- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n   347\t  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n   348\t  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   349\t  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n   350\t  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n   351\t  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n   352\t  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n   353\t  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n   354\t- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n   355\t  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n   356\t  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n   357\t  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n   358\t  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n   359\t  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n   360\t  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n   361\t  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n   362\t  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n   363\t- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n   364\t  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n   365\t  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n   366\t  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n   367\t  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n   368\t  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n   369\t  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n   370\t- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n   371\t  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n   372\t  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n   373\t  another class, the call is doing several jobs: move the rule to its owner (a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field)\n   374\t  rather than add a sentence (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你这些修改都是失败的呀，为什么，根因，你要检讨然后再接着尝试。我觉得你已经陷入deep loop 了\").\n   375\t  A failed step of a plan is fixed and re-run at that same step: its failures are the work list, and nothing later in the plan and no\n   376\t  substitute plan starts before it passes (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"你为什么要drift? 你现在明明还有这么多的问题要fix,你到底知不知道你要fix什么？\").\n   377\t  Before a fix is proposed, write which goal the mechanism still serves and what the product already gives for it; a measurement that\n   378\t  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\n   379\t  it and you're giving me suggestions that you reject yourself\").\n   380\t- **Before a version is rejected, the rejection is checked.** Every failed or refused answer behind a \"did not pass\" is read against its\n   381\t  source and put down as the model's error or the measuring rule's or check's error; a rule or check that refuses right answers is fixed,\n   382\t  and a version that already meets the goal (what it was built to fix is fixed, nothing that was right turned wrong) is not dropped for a\n   383\t  stricter rule a later review added. Alex, 2026-11-05: \"你到底是不是再搬石头砸自己的脚？各种reject自己，你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\";\n   384\t  \"你不能每次都这样判错然后浪费我时间，我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\".\n   385\t- **Correct, then cheap.** Make the pipeline right and stable before any cost, speed or throughput work; report cost as a baseline only\n   386\t  (Alex, 2026-10-25).\n   387\t\n   388\t## 8. Product thinking\n  3711\t## D355 · 2026-11-04 · The filing topic closes without a change: filing is about 85% right; the remaining misses are recorded as known defects\n  3712\t\n  3713\t- Alex opened the topic on 2026-11-03 (\"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\"),\n  3714\t  set the method on 2026-11-04 (\"We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we\n  3715\t  dive into do the full analysis stability test\"; \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"), and closed it: \"那就1吧\"\n  3716\t  (option 1: close the topic, record the pattern as a known defect, go to step 5).\n  3717\t- What was found (`research/2026-11-03-filing/report.html`, `log.md` rows 1–17): three rounds of Claude–Codex review converged on \"the question\n  3718\t  definition is too narrow\"; an independent challenge and the first stored-request test refuted it (the earlier version's definition was already\n 11145\t    - trillions are compared with billions.\n 11146\t  - Model errors in the sample: a growth rate supported by forecasts computed from it (a cycle), and two commitments added without\n 11147\t    an established overlap.\n 11148\t- **Process error (Claude's):**\n 11149\t  - The $0 gate's passing answer was written knowing the check's ids, units and spellings. It proved the harness, not the request.\n 11150\t    The missed step is an answer written by a reader who sees only the outgoing request, run through the real checks (AGENTS §6,\n 11151\t    \"Check before the send\").\n 11152\t  - Council rounds 47–47h reviewed the harness and never the request against the check.\n 11153\t  - The mid-run diagnosis named the wrong field (`rests_on`).\n 11154\t- **Council consensus, round 48** (`claude-r48.md`, `codex-r48.md`):\n 11155\t  - Keep the STOP. One recommendation for Alex: a bounded repair of judging-v13's request and checks.\n 11156\t    - Each field's rule goes beside the field, with enums for ids, units and choices where the schema can hold them.\n 11157\t    - The demonstrated period, arithmetic, parser and unit failures are fixed. The checks for scope changes, unstated assumptions\n 11158\t      and cycles stay.\n 11159\t  - The test is $0: a registered blind conformance test.\n 11160\t    - Correct examples and planted defects are fixed first. An independent writer sees only the new request, and their first\n 11161\t      outputs go through the real harness unedited.\n 11162\t    - The test stops if a correct form is refused, a planted defect passes, or the writer needs an unstated rule.\n 11163\t    - Only then is a re-send of the same 36 requests asked for, under a new decision with D725's lines unchanged.\n 11164\t  - Claude's lean, a code-built catalogue of source expressions, was set aside: parser omissions would become missing evidence, and\n 11165\t    the catalogue leaves the outcome link untouched.\n 11166\t  - The alternative is to close judging-v13. poc-v118 stays the product (D690), and the number answers stay a known defect.\n 11167\t- **Next:** Alex chooses between the repair and closing. Nothing is changed or sent before his answer.\n 11168\t\n 11169\t## D734 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: repair judging-v13's request and checks once, then a $0 blind conformance test\n 11170\t\n 11171\t- **The question** (after D733): \"判数字的新版本（一次判一组相关的数）花钱那一关没过：72 个答案全被挡在“填格式”这一步。原因是填写规则只写在检查代码里、没写进给模型的说明，而且检查代码自己也会把对的判错。这没回答“一起判会不会更准”。下一步怎么走？\"\n 11172\t  Options:\n 11173\t  - 修一次再零成本盲测 (recommended);\n 11174\t  - 关掉这条线.\n 11175\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"修一次再零成本盲测 (推荐)\".\n 11176\t- **Decided (Alex):** one bounded repair of judging-v13's request and checks, per council round 48 (D733).\n 11177\t  - Each field's rule goes beside its field, with enums where the schema can hold them.\n 11178\t  - The demonstrated check failures are fixed, and the checks for scope changes, unstated assumptions and cycles are kept.\n 11179\t  - Then a registered $0 blind conformance test, with its stop conditions. Nothing is paid or sent.\n 11180\t  - A clean result goes back to Alex as a request to re-send the same 36 requests under a new decision, with D725's lines\n 11181\t    unchanged. A stop goes back to him with its census.\n 11182\t- **The order of the work (AGENTS §2, §7.3):** the repair design with its tables, then council rounds until one finds nothing\n 11183\t  serious, then code with tests and mutants. The test is registered before it runs, with its examples fixed first.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
