{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D72[12]|retire|mechanism exists' AGENTS.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n 'R[234]|C[389]|G[34]|constructed|mutant' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/GATE-RESULT.md\"","aggregated_output":"AGENTS.md:147:- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\nAGENTS.md:378:  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\nAGENTS.md:490:2. `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` holds the status, the open defects and the one next task; a status update retires the paragraphs it replaces.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:921:  - The wording scope (D36) covers the views database and the labels node; the retired words are 驱动, 检验条件 (证实条件,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1463:     (already retired in the pull mode PRD) and sending a view on a disagreement within a tier (replaced by D38).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2059:| New answer or dataset | Validate known IDs before rendering; retire graph nodes no longer loaded. |\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2335:- The writer owns the replacement rule (06-views, the Replace row): a piece may replace one in force only with a stated day not earlier than the stored one's, a tier at least the stored one's (fact and party statement above third-party view above rumour), and, between two third-party views, the same party; otherwise it is stored as new. Found when Jev's `supersedes` let analysts' reactions retire reported facts (log rows 39–41); the rule applies to both matching engines.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2356:- Removed: the retired research harness `poc/hierarchy_study/` (17 experiments and 15 test files, D146–D162, none adopted; its tests wrote three SQLite files to the repository root through a module-named path, also removed); five finished one-off scripts (`jev_poc.py`, `supersedes_probe.py`, `succession_probe.py`, `key_views.py`, `review_keyed_run.py`; results in the build log and `poc/reports/`); six product functions with no caller (`judging.judge_one`, `matching.same_orientation`, `Universe.canonical_scope`, `testdb.days_with_items`, `store.lineage_of_view`, `store.replaced_by`) and six unused constants.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2566:- Also in this slice, from the stall at 2026-08-07: a code-refused judgement answer is retired from the archive's lookup (`model.Archive.retire`; the row stays; schema-refused and malformed rows already carried a suffix), so a resume re-samples instead of replaying the refused answer; and the request's closing line names a closed set that exists (\"cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis\"; \"a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views\"): 4 of the run's 5 retried first answers had put theme ids into cites_views.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2592:- Measured ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md), 2026-10-27 23:05–23:30, $0.24): the 24-case gold was written, then re-read as a hedge-fund analyst's standard (eight rules in `gold.md`, Alex: \"做一个 hedge fund analyst 的专业视角去看怎么做这一步的标准\"). One send per case of the new path (step 2 reader → Jev opinions → one gpt-6-luna call with the complete context): step 4 places and merges right on 20 of 21 development and 3 of 3 held-out cases, never retires a different statement; two misses (G09 the denial not written into the argument, G11 a bank's echo taken as independent). Jev's piece opinions are right on 7 of 18; the product's replace class has its mechanism in the `supersedes` criterion (\"an official confirms or denies that reported claim\"): re-sending the 47 stored replacements, 16 do not reproduce and 7 flip to a `contradicts` class once the clause is split out. Two harness contradictions of the assistant's (a check refusing what the prompt asked; the record's own id) were fixed at $0, and nine gold rows were corrected from verified ledger ids (the gold had been written from a ranked excerpt, not the complete expansion). No production change yet: the writer still acts on Jev's label.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2594:## D202 · 2026-10-27 · The writer retires nothing on a matching label: a replacement is recorded as a revision and both pieces stay in force\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2596:- Alex, on the arm1 result and the proposal: \"你接着做，需要非常严谨的看结果和测量\". Census first ([labels](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/replacements-47-labels.json), every pair read): of the run's 47 retirements, 22 are the owner's later value or status of the same claim (right under rule E), 20 retired a statement that should have stayed (10 a contradiction or qualification, among them a denial erasing the delay report, \"subject to final agreements\" erasing the $500bn announcement; 10 a different matter), 5 were restatements mislabelled. Jev's `supersedes` label does not separate them: 17 of 22 right and 12 of 20 wrong carry it; with \"confirms or denies\" split out (`jev_contradicts.py`) 4 wrong ones flip to `contradicts` but so do 3 right ones. No label the matcher gives is safe to retire on.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2608:- D201 measured further ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md), 2026-10-28 00:00–01:20, $0.85): a fresh 16-case gold written from the complete expansions before any send (action 11/12 and 4/4 held out; nothing wrongly retired 16/16; same-claim 8/12 with one class: a second outlet's own reporting treated as independent, which the contract could not express); arm 2 split claim identity from source independence (the class is gone; two new judgement weaknesses appeared); three draws per disagreeing case under both prompts show the arm-to-arm differences are within one draw's noise, while in 144 draws no must-not-touch piece was ever marked same or revised. Decided: the contract keeps arm 2's split; prompt arms stop here; the variable fields are annotations under D202 and the next build is the argument record (steps 5 and 6), where a wrong relation in one draw is corrected by the next instead of being frozen into the ledger.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2635:- Measured: core statements filed right 6/6/5 → 9/9/9 (with six seeded driver questions shown) and 9/10/9 under the old rule; wrong links 9 → 3; links to the two sinks 63/60/44 → 6/1/5; junk placed 53/48/32 → 39/27/35; every decisive matter statement (the Kyber/Rubin Ultra rack delay cluster, the AI Compute Partnership participants, Goldman's capex estimate) placed; one week through the whole path (`english-v36-nvda-1w-2026-10-28`, $0.22 against $0.22) kept 580 statements the old path dropped. Arms retired by measurement: the extraction's links shown as a hint (junk and sink links returned), group aliases alone (the groups lack the press names). Tests `tests/test_placement.py`, suite 222.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3005:## D254 · 2026-11-01 · Placement: a question's code-written 'takes' line is the one rule for its file; D207's \"company-wide figure questions take only their own figures\" is retired\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3151:## D274 · 2026-11-03 · The extraction production prompt is frozen at v74i (`poc-v108`); the unadopted variants are retired\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3159:- Retired, never run as a stored run and never a default, backed up first (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/retired-2026-11-03/retired-variants.tar.gz`,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3330:- Keep confidence, weights, calculation and thesis explanations unchanged. The help popup shows the same explanation on hover or keyboard focus, with wrapped text inside the detail panel. Update the retired table assertions to verify calculation separately and the new weight pills/help markup. Verify the actual drawer and existing UI suite; no model, date or database change.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3665:- Also retired: the parallel-day study runners (`poc/concurrency_study/budget.py`, `e2e.py`, `full_day.py`, `multi_day.py`) and the two\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3737:     premises, triggers) is retired. Config's `final_verdict` setting stays in the frozen configurations (D274) and is read by no step.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3763:## D357 · 2026-11-04 · Clean the repository of configurations and prompts nothing current names; the code paths of retired versions are a slice of their own\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3779:- Not done in this slice: the code paths that only retired prompt versions take (version gates in `extraction.py` and `views/judging.py`)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3800:- Alex, on Claude's list of the two open cleanup items (the old worktrees, and the code paths only retired prompt versions take, with the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3811:  naming another version is refused before any request (`require_supported`). The answer checks are unchanged except what only retired\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3820:  retired versions left with them, the rest now run on `poc-v108`); the frozen-file tests, the UI tests and `docs/check.py` pass.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3822:  [Open questions] block and replays the answer against them, reads items as the feed does (`testdb.item_of`), counts a row of a retired\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3825:- **Files retired** (Git keeps them): 41 configurations and 80 prompt files that no code, test, script or UI file loads, among them the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3828:  and scripts load, and `poc-v22` (read by `scripts/recall_oracle.py`). The backup manifest of D274's retired variants is restored beside\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4009:- Present and forward-looking financial performance, estimates and guidance need to be tracked as evidence relevant to investment questions; a quarterly period is not itself a reason to withhold information from a related annual question. Do not confuse retaining and connecting evidence with automatically opening a separate question for every line. The research model continues to judge relevance and the strength of the connection; do not hard-code company, item or metric-specific importance. Existing research questions remain context; the separate report import and 22 preset questions remain retired under D370.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4236:  D370's retirement of them as a starting library) is part of that question.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4895:- **Correction, 2026-11-13:** \"production as it now runs\" is `poc-v118` (D370, D374, the replay default; `scripts/replay.py` refuses `poc-v116`, which carries the retired baseline block). D442's \"poc-v116\" above is a factual error of mine; the decision means v118, as D431 says (\"production as it now runs\").\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6426:  before that day's judging round can be rebuilt and verified against the stored run, the retired preset questions accounted\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7244:- **Evidence after the final change:** the adapter's tests 34 (the retired guard's two tests replaced; two launcher tests moved to\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10150:## D682 · 2026-11-20 · Under D681 (council): J2a and J2b retired; the carried previous conclusion is the lead mechanism; a separating test on complete evidence\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10166:  - retire J2a and J2b;\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10180:  - **The 432-card blind reading:** J2a holds 2 of 24 targets and J2b 4 of 24, against a locked floor of 12 and a net of 8. Both are retired\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10220:  - Result: **0 net repairs against 2 required.** No control was lost, no refusals, and both plants were caught. **H1 is retired.**\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10614:  1–3, now written) paired with three fresh controls (poc-v118, the readers' old judgements retired by reader and day from each link's\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10859:## D721 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 43/43b: the double-count premise is partly falsified by the frozen gold; recommend closing the design with nothing to build; D711's H4 reading corrected\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10892:## D722 · 2026-11-22 · Alex closes the double-count design with nothing changed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10894:- **The question** (after D721): \"'总收入把 CPU 又加一遍'这件事，按冻结金标的推理不算错：金标自己就把 CPU 目标当成总收入超过共识的理由之一。我和 Codex 都建议把这个修法设计收尾，什么都不改。你怎么定？\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10902:  - D721's findings stay a list, not a work order.\n5:- **Mutants** (`mutants.py`, `mutants.log`): 47 of 47 caught; the unmutated control passes.\n12:  - a segment quarter above the company quarter (C3);\n15:  - a scope conversion with no stated assumption (C8);\n28:| 1 | 28 | FAIL (G3) | the per-unit identity added (a general identity, not fitted to the case) |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport collections, json, pathlib\nroot=pathlib.Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers\\\")\npaid=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22\\\")\nplan=json.loads((root/\\\"paid-plan.json\\\").read_text())\nfor p in plan:\n print(p[\\\"unit\\\"],p[\\\"arm\\\"],len(json.dumps(p[\\\"schema\\\"])),len(p[\\\"evidence_ids\\\"]),len(p[\\\"user\\\"]),len(p[\\\"system\\\"]),len(p[\\\"family\\\"][\\\"relations\\\"]),len(p[\\\"family\\\"][\\\"compare_periods\\\"]))\nfor name in [\\\"answers.jsonl\\\",\\\"retries.jsonl\\\"]:\n rows=[json.loads(line) for line in (paid/name).read_text().splitlines()]\n print(name,collections.Counter(r.get(\\\"status\\\") for r in rows))\n for r in rows:\n  if r.get(\\\"status\\\")==\\\"answered\\\":\n   print({k:type(v).__name__ for k,v in r.items()})\n   break\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
