{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '75,91p;108,116p;216,225p;326,347p'\"","aggregated_output":"    75\t   build it as the fix. A fix that another change subsumes is not built.\n    76\t\n    77\tBefore any design: ten raw answers read beside their inputs, the whole request read as the model reads it, and, for a choice the model\n    78\tmade, the model's own account (continue the stored conversation with \"which instruction led you here, and which two statements did you\n    79\treject\", a cent a case).\n    80\t\n    81\tThen converge or stop:\n    82\t- A mechanism named on its counted class is fixed in the same slice and measured, and the report leads with it. A root-caused defect is\n    83\t  never parked \"for Alex\"; a parked fix is an open defect. Go to Alex only when the mechanism is not found, or the fix would change the\n    84\t  measuring stick or the PRD.\n    85\t- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.\n    86\t- A failure called a flake is a defect until traced. Read a failing check to its first differing line before any rerun; a passing rerun\n    87\t  proves nothing.\n    88\t- A subagent's or reviewer's report is a lead. Read the code, contract or record it rests on before acting on it or recording it, and\n    89\t  cite what you read, not the summary (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你找到的这些问题验证是真的问题吗？\").\n    90\t\n    91\t## 2. Before writing code: design\n   108\t\n   109\t- A contract over text or shapes states the closed set of what passes (a full match); anything else fails or is not judged. Enumerate\n   110\t  the accepted set against every context and reader it meets before the first edit.\n   111\t- **Code owns identity, never importance.** Before building a closed list, enum or gate, write which decision it takes from the model\n   112\t  and whether that decision is identity (\"are these the same thing?\") or judgement (\"does this matter?\"); build only the identity part.\n   113\t  A list of what matters is at most a hint shown to the model (Alex, 2026-10-25: \"你这个做法难道不是非常的限死吗？永远都是一堆财务指标，真正的观点呢？\").\n   114\t- **No case-fitted fix.** A hand list, a special path or a rule fitted to the case in view fixes that case and breaks the next. First ask\n   115\t  whether the judge had the material and the definition it needed, and whether a typed field is missing; run the proposal against the\n   116\t  existing tests and the gold for a counter-example before building (D167: \"我不要 hardcode 解法 it's premature optimization, not general root fix\").\n   216\t  products or its numbers, and none is taken from a test article. A fix is written from the standard and from the request read as the\n   217\t  model reads it, not from the bench's misses, and a prompt is scrubbed for one-company or one-industry wording before any measurement.\n   218\t  Alex, 2026-10-29 (D237): \"It needs to be general purpose as a hedge fund brain. I keep on telling you this, and you keep on cherry\n   219\t  picking the results just to meet the metrics or the benchmarks\".\n   220\t- **Never grow a prompt to fix quality.** Read the whole request (system, schema, payload) as the model reads it, and list every\n   221\t  contradiction, rule written for another case, instruction that forces the defect, reference the model cannot read, payload field the\n   222\t  answer does not need, and call doing several jobs. Cut, merge or split. Add an instruction only when the audit shows one is missing,\n   223\t  and remove at least as much elsewhere. Report characters and prompt tokens before and after; growth needs a written reason.\n   224\t- **Trace a miss to the raw answer first.** Class it as not written, refused (by which check) or split. Check that the request shows what\n   225\t  the answer needs and the schema can express it before changing any wording.\n   326\t### 7.3 Iterating\n   327\t\n   328\t- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n   329\t  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n   330\t  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n   331\t  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n   332\t- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n   333\t  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n   334\t  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n   335\t  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n   336\t- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n   337\t  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n   338\t  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n   339\t- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n   340\t  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n   341\t- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n   342\t  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n   343\t  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n   344\t  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n   345\t  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n   346\t- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n   347\t  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r48.md | tail -n 12; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r49.md | tail -n 8'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r48.md | tail -n 12; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r49.md | tail -n 8'","aggregated_output":"    62\t\n    63\t## 3. Why the zero-cost gate missed it\n    64\t\n    65\t**The author of the passing answer already knew the checker’s rules.** The fixtures hand in the expected IDs, units and period spellings. The paid rehearsal’s clean answer goes further and uses an estimate inside a preselected rung, with no source calculation and an unavailable reference. That proves the harness can carry a conforming answer and that planted defects can trigger checks. It leaves unanswered whether someone reading the exact request could write a conforming answer without that inside knowledge. [Registered controls](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:152) · [Clean rehearsal fixture](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_rehearsal.py:42)\n    66\t\n    67\tThe missed step was a **blind write-and-check using the exact outgoing request**. Give an independent writer only the system text, user text and schema. Have them encode real forecasts and then run their first outputs through the actual harness. For each refusal, ask the writer to point to where the request stated the rule. Read the check back in the other direction for correct answers it cannot represent. An evidence ID enum would have prevented the most common source mistake. The request already uses one for citations. [AGENTS §6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:231) · [AGENTS §7.3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:370) · [Sent schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json:120)\n    68\t\n    69\t## 4. One recommendation and one test\n    70\t\n    71\t**Recommendation.** Keep the STOP and ask Alex to open one bounded repair of the judging-v13 request and checker. Put each field’s rule next to the field. Use enums for known IDs, units and choices where the schema can enforce them. Fix the demonstrated arithmetic, period and source-boundary failures while preserving checks for genuine scope changes, unsupported assumptions and circular calculations. Code already extracts numeric expressions for verification. Sending a complete catalog of those expressions to the model could remove some copying, but would also make today’s parser omissions into missing evidence. It would leave the universal outcome-link failure untouched. Closing v13 now would save further work, but the result has not answered D725’s question about shared calculations. One bounded test can determine whether there is a workable way to express those calculations at all. [D725](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10957) · [D690](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10360)\n    72\t\n    73\t**Test.** Run one blind conformance test at $0 on fresh examples covering a joint pair, its two separate replies, and all three singleton calculation shapes. Before the test, register correct examples and deliberately broken counterparts, including a wrong number, a wrong period or scope, an unresolved overlap and a circular calculation. Run the independent writer’s first replies through the real harness without hand edits. **Stop if any correct form is refused, any planted defect gets through its intended check, or the reader still needs an unwritten rule to encode a correct answer.** Use the 72 stored replies to check individual fixes where the intended figure and source are identifiable. A guessed link or rewritten answer earns no credit. A clean result earns a request to rerun the same 36-call comparison under a fresh decision, with the original pass lines. The current gate’s STOP stands. [Registered reading and stop rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:250)    42\t\n    43\t## Build and record\n    44\t\n    45\t- **The rehearsal must read the new plan, and the old run must keep its reader.** The rehearsal loads `paid-plan.json` at import and validates outgoing bytes against that object. Updating stubs alone still rehearses the old schema. The equivalent repair run should consume a separately pinned plan and compare it with the old plan by case, evidence, questions, family data and intended request changes. The old journals store the raw old shape. Replacing `strip` everywhere would reinterpret those entries during packet rendering and recovery. Recovery also rewrites `results.json`. Bind decoding and checking to the plan version and verify historical reproduction on a copy. I confirmed the current plan hash matches its pin, the run’s plan has identical data, and the current builder recreates the exact original plan bytes. [Rehearsal plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_rehearsal.py:18) · [Byte comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_rehearsal.py:120) · [Recovery and send pin](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:365)\n    46\t\n    47\t- **9,624 characters is one old schema’s size.** Across the 12 stored cases, schemas were **5,652–10,056 characters** and user messages **13,202–134,199 characters**. The 36 scored calls used **5,534–38,797 input tokens** each. Copying the evidence enum adds up to about **2,332 serialized characters** before new descriptions, and the enum already appears in `cites` and `pushes`. Use one schema definition for passage IDs if the strict request path accepts it. Report whole-request characters, estimated tokens and maximum size before and after. Write the actual field descriptions into the design for review now. Keep the paid examples as tests and use examples from other domains in the request. [Size proposal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:167) · [Repeated passage enum](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:61) · [Prompt size rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:220)\n    48\t\n    49\t**Recommendation:** bring back one revised design with the exact schema wording and corrected case list. The decisive $0 test is to send the registered good and bad forms through the same schema, converter and checks the gate uses, then read the blind writers’ first answers against those same rules and passages.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py | sed -n '98,116p'; rg -n -m 4 '65% growth in Q4|12% sequential' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json | cut -c1-350\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py | sed -n '98,116p'; rg -n -m 4 '65% growth in Q4|12% sequential' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json | cut -c1-350\"","aggregated_output":"    98\t            if eid not in seen:\n    99\t                seen.add(eid)\n   100\t                lines.append('- ' + item)\n   101\t        themes = themes or next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Themes')), '')\n   102\t        prev = next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Previous')), '').split('\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema')[0]   # [46g.1] v7's output line goes\n   103\t        earlier.append(f'- {view_id}: ' + prev.replace('[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]', 'our earlier forecast, not a source:').strip())\n   104\t    rel = '; '.join(f'{r[\"part\"]} is part of {r[\"whole\"]}' if r['type'] == 'part_of' else f'{r[\"later\"]} rests on {r[\"earlier\"]}\\'s base'\n   105\t                    for r in family['relations'] if {r.get('part'), r.get('whole'), r.get('later'), r.get('earlier')} - {None} <= shown) or 'none'\n   106\t    shared = '; '.join(f'{w[\"population\"]}, {w[\"measure\"]}, {w[\"scope\"]}, {w[\"period\"]}' for w in family['shared']) or 'none'\n   107\t    keys = '; '.join(f'{v} = {m[\"what\"][\"population\"]} | {m[\"what\"][\"measure\"]} | {m[\"what\"][\"scope\"]} | {m[\"what\"][\"period\"]}'\n   108\t                     for v, m in family.get('members', {}).items() if v in shown)\n   109\t    user = ('[Family] members:\\n' + '\\n\\n'.join(heads) + f'\\n\\nRelations: {rel}.\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: {shared}.\\n'\n   110\t            + (f'Outcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), to be used exactly: {keys}.\\n' if keys else '') + '\\n'\n   111\t            f'[Evidence in view for the family, {len(lines)} items]\\n' + '\\n'.join(lines) + '\\n\\n' + themes\n   112\t            + '\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.')   # D728: no earlier forecast\n   113\t    return user, sorted(seen), [t.split(' ', 1)[0] for t in themes.split('\\n- ')[1:]]\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\tdef strict(calc, schema):\n11:  \"user\": \"[Family] members:\\nThesis v4 (NVDA, asset, focus \\\"NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027\\\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: Total revenue is at least $431.2 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: Total revenue is at least $392 billion and below $431.2 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: To\n1467:    \"text\": \"Management projects revenues of around $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, up 12% sequentially at the midpoint.\",\n1567:    \"text\": \"and 65% growth in Q4.\",\n1939:    \"text\": \"Looking ahead, NVIDIA expects profitability to remain strong and projects revenues to reach $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, up 12% sequentially from the midpoint.\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"**Finish the one repair Alex already approved, then run one $0 blind test.** In the paid run, Luna wrote forecasts such as “$398.1 billion” where the checker expected the ID of a figure. The request never said so. That mismatch alone affected all 90 member answers. Round 49 shows the draft repair needs revision. It has yet to test whether Luna can use a fully stated format. [Paid result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md:20) · [D734](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11169)\n\n### 1. The repair is bounded if we give it a finish line\n\nClaude is right about the defects in the draft. A model can relabel a 12% sequential rate as year-over-year growth and make the proposed growth check accept it. The proposed quote check can read `−12%` as `+12%`. The growth fix needs proof of the comparison period from the shown source or from the calculation’s inputs. Where that proof is missing, the conversion is an assumption. The quote fix needs to preserve signs and qualifiers in context. Both have concrete good and bad examples to test. [Round 49 counterexamples](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r49.md:5)\n\nClaude’s **58** counts refusal messages. Several express the same rule, and some apply only to particular operations or to earlier forecasts that the outgoing schema already excludes. I estimate **16,000–20,000 characters for the largest repaired schema and its family-specific instructions**, up from about 10,000 for the largest stored schema. That allows roughly 3,000–5,000 characters for figure forms and operations, 1,000–2,000 for rules shared across figures, and up to 2,332 for passage IDs if they must be repeated. This is a writing estimate. In the saved replies, joint first attempts had **13–22 figures, with a median of 16**. That is enough repetition for small mistakes to sink a reply even when the instructions fit. [Schema inventory](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r49.md:15) · [Stored sizes](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r49.md:47) · [First attempts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/answers.jsonl)\n\nI would allow **two further review rounds**, one on the exact wording and corrected examples, then one on the request the harness actually sends and the checks it runs. After that, run the blind test once. If a serious issue remains after the second review, return it to Alex. D355 calls for a stop when the evidence contradicts the hypothesis. D734 was written after the paid stop and explicitly puts design review before the blind test. [D355](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3711) · [D734](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11176)\n\n### 2. The six checks miss two things the product needs\n\n| Defect | What needs to catch it |\n|---|---|\n| A segment exceeds the total, or the model adds a segment already included in the total | **C3** catches the first, such as Data Center Q4 at $146B against company Q4 at $127B. **C8** is needed for the second. I checked a $100B total plus its $30B segment in memory. C8 refused it until I added `stated_in_addition`, then accepted $130B with no evidence or recorded assumption. Correct arithmetic and a part below its whole can coexist with double counting. If inclusion is genuinely uncertain, show what changes when the disputed amount is removed. [Stored cases](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:154) · [C8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:407) |\n| Two forecasts for one quarter | **C4** must check what each answer actually uses. The stored example has one $113.5B forecast, yet the segment calculation goes straight to the $108B guide. Counting forecast entries alone would pass it. [Stored Q3 example](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:157) |\n| The system’s forecast is presented as the market’s | **C5** must follow the calculation back to shown outside sources. An outside citation beside an internal estimate cannot make the estimate external. [Reference check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:779) |\n| A source number is misread, or the arithmetic is wrong | **C1** needs to preserve the value, unit, sign and qualifier. **C2** needs to recompute the result. Both depend on **C7**, which checks that links resolve, the number answers the right question, and the calculation has no cycle. A paid retry actually used a growth rate to compute forecasts that it then cited as support for that same rate. [Source check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:78) · [Paid cycle](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r48.md:56) |\n\n**C6, checking that the forecast overlaps the selected band, is the one check in Claude’s six that the five defects do not require.** It serves a separate purpose in the current answer design and should stay in this repair. Outside the six, C7 and the identity checks in C8 are essential. The specific per-unit formula preserves a valid gate example, and the balance-plus-flows format represents the real $25B plus $18B commitments case. [Band rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:75) · [Gate findings](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/GATE-RESULT.md:9)\n\nThe **10% midpoint perturbation in C9** and the deep scenario-routing variants were developed on constructed examples. The underlying rules still matter when a family declares a common base or compares scenarios. The paid families never declare `same_base`, so this run tells us nothing about the value of that particular perturbation test. **C10’s earlier-answer pointer** is the clearest case of a mechanism whose job was removed from the outgoing request by D728. The schema excludes earlier forecasts, while C5 still protects the market reference. [C9 and C10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:599) · [Paid family declarations](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:63) · [D728](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11041)\n\n### 3. Option B needs Alex’s decision\n\nB keeps the labelled figures, shared calculation and unresolved answer. It changes what the system can publish. For example, `730 ÷ 800 × 1,300` can be calculated correctly while mixing different companies, types of spending and years. The current design requires the conversion to be stated as an assumption. Readers decide whether that assumption is supported. B as written would move the requirement to state it out of the checks. That changes the design and exceeds D734. [D725](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10975) · [Stored scope example](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:159) · [Claude’s option B](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r49.md:50)\n\n### 4. One test for Alex\n\n**Run the repaired request through one registered $0 blind test.** Fix the archived inputs first. The proposed Vera case is a Fed question, and the spending case asks about calendar 2026. Use a joint pair, its two separate requests, and the three singleton shapes, with at least one case containing new evidence that changes the calculation. Register correct forms and deliberately broken versions first. Two independent writers get only the exact outgoing request, in a fresh context for each case. Run their first answers through the real harness unedited and read them against the passages. [Input and test findings](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r49.md:37)\n\n**Stop** if a correct form is refused, a planted error escapes its intended check, a writer needs an unstated rule, the run is incomplete, or any case registered as answerable yields zero usable first replies. The joint case must yield both supported forecasts in the same reply. A justified unresolved answer counts on a case registered to exercise that outcome. A pass earns a request to Alex for the paid comparison. It takes that later run to measure whether Luna can do this at medium effort in one pass. This review used saved requests and read-only probes. [Proposed blind test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:139) · [D734](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11176)"}}
{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{"input_tokens":1313054,"cached_input_tokens":1207424,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7129,"reasoning_output_tokens":2276}}
